{"metadata":{"url":"https://github.com/terryyin/lizard/pull/532","number":532,"state":"open","merged":false,"mergeable":true,"draft":false,"body":"### The problem\n\nA parameter is counted only if its name starts with a letter and is not one of\nthe TypeScript type keywords, so these functions have one parameter each:\n\n```ts\nfunction render(text, _key, $el) { return 1; }\nfunction round(number: number, precision: number): number { return 1; }\n```\n\n```\n$ lizard a.ts          # master, 01afe9c\n       1      1     12      1       1 render@1-1@a.ts\n       1      1     16      1       1 round@2-2@a.ts\n```\n\n`_key` and `$el` are valid names, and so is `number`: the keyword filter was\nthere to skip the type after the colon, but it skips a parameter with the same\nname too.\n\n### What changes\n\nOnly `lizard_languages/javascript_functions.py`. A parameter is now any\nidentifier, `$` included, and the tokens after the colon of a parameter, up to\nthe next parameter, are its type and are skipped, which makes the keyword list\nunnecessary. With the fix:\n\n```\n       1      1     12      3       1 render@1-1@a.ts\n       1      1     16      2       1 round@2-2@a.ts\n```\n\n### How it is tested\n\nA test in `test/test_languages/testJavaScriptFunctions.py` for `_` and `$`,\nand one in `test/test_languages/testTypeScriptMetrics.py` for parameters named\nas a type keyword; both fail on `master` without the change. The full suite\npasses on the branch: `python -m pytest test` gives 1667 passed, 7 skipped.\npycodestyle reports no new warnings in the changed files.\n\n### What does not change\n\nA parameter named `$` alone is still not counted: the common parameter list of\nlizard keeps only names made of word characters. #535 builds on\nthis one.\n\nThanks for maintaining lizard and for taking the time to look at this.\n","title":"Count JavaScript/TypeScript parameters named with \"_\", \"$\" or a type keyword","base":"master","base_sha":"01afe9c228ba2a3dc5253259d8415d2ef47f0b71","head":"pr/js-parameter-names","head_sha":"d0713bf5b4dcf4bf24453156a3756688627abbc0","head_repo_id":1401695752,"head_repo_full_name":"FabioMalpezzi/lizard","merge_commit_sha":"1a6e343430a7e7c0d546c97da1c60cbb1d86eb7d","user":{"login":"FabioMalpezzi","name":"FabioMalpezzi","email":null,"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/102038548?v=4","id":102038548},"requested_reviewers":null,"requested_team_reviewers":null,"diff":null,"comments":null,"created_at":"2026-10-26T23:16:47Z","updated_at":"2026-10-26T23:17:14Z","closed_at":null,"merged_at":null,"commits":1,"changed_files":3,"additions":27,"deletions":14,"display_url":"https://github.com/terryyin/lizard/pull/532","display_title":"Count JavaScript/TypeScript parameters named with \"_\", \"$\" or a type keyword"},"jobs":{"jobs":[{"id":121907184307,"name":"build (ubuntu-24.04, 3.10)","status":"completed","conclusion":"success","run_id":40418648778,"logs_url":null,"steps":[{"name":"Set up job","status":"completed","conclusion":"success","number":1},{"name":"Run actions/checkout@v3","status":"completed","conclusion":"success","number":2},{"name":"Set up Python","status":"completed","conclusion":"success","number":3},{"name":"Install dependencies","status":"completed","conclusion":"success","number":4},{"name":"build and Install","status":"completed","conclusion":"success","number":5},{"name":"Run tests","status":"completed","conclusion":"success","number":6},{"name":"Post Set up Python","status":"completed","conclusion":"success","number":11},{"name":"Post Run actions/checkout@v3","status":"completed","conclusion":"success","number":12},{"name":"Complete job","status":"completed","conclusion":"success","number":13}]},{"id":121907184623,"name":"build (windows-latest, 3.8)","status":"completed","conclusion":"success","run_id":40418648778,"logs_url":null,"steps":[{"name":"Set up job","status":"completed","conclusion":"success","number":1},{"name":"Run actions/checkout@v3","status":"completed","concl